  VERDICT: CONFIRMED

  ## 1. `hideStepperAndActions` prop and both `deliveryActions` render sites — index.tsx

  Type declaration, `overrides/app/components/product-item/index.tsx:123`:
  ```ts
  hideStepperAndActions?: boolean;
  ```
  Optional boolean, confirmed. Destructured with a falsy default at line 146: `hideStepperAndActions = false,`.

  **Both `deliveryActions` render sites found and both are gated:**

  Site 1 (mobile-hidden desktop delivery-actions row), lines 174–176:
  ```tsx
  {!hideStepperAndActions && deliveryActions && !product.bonusProductLineItem && (
    <HideOnMobile>{deliveryActions}</HideOnMobile>
  )}
  ```

  Site 2 (desktop-hidden mobile delivery-actions row), lines 179–181:
  ```tsx
  {!hideStepperAndActions && deliveryActions && !product.bonusProductLineItem && (
    <HideOnDesktop>{deliveryActions}</HideOnDesktop>
  )}
  ```

  Both carry the identical `!hideStepperAndActions &&` guard — this is the exact bug shape the task asked me to hunt for (one site gated, one not), and it is not present.

  Other gated sites, all confirmed present:
  - Stepper (`BonusProductQuantity`/`ProductQuantityPicker`), line 185: `{!hideStepperAndActions && !(isRemoving && product.bonusProductLineItem) && (...)}`
  - `primaryAction`, two sites, both gated: line 203 `{!hideStepperAndActions && <HideOnMobile>{primaryAction}</HideOnMobile>}` and lines 221–225 `{!hideStepperAndActions && (<HideOnDesktop><Box w={'full'}>{primaryAction}</Box></HideOnDesktop>)}`
  - `secondaryActions`, line 217: `{!hideStepperAndActions && secondaryActions}`

  Confirmed via full-file read plus a targeted grep (`grep -n "deliveryActions\|hideStepperAndActions\|primaryAction\|secondaryActions"`) — no ungated render site for any of the four surfaces exists anywhere in the file.

  ## 2. index.test.tsx — both required tests exist, both are real DOM assertions

  **(a) Suppression test**, lines 161–187 (`'hideStepperAndActions suppresses the stepper and every actions surface, and nothing throws'`):
  ```tsx
  expect(() =>
    renderWithProviders(
      <ProductItem
        product={MOCK_LINE_ITEM}
        primaryAction={<button type="button">Remove</button>}
        secondaryActions={<button type="button">Edit</button>}
        deliveryActions={<span>Ship to store</span>}
        hideStepperAndActions
      />,
    ),
  ).not.toThrow();

  expect(screen.queryByText('Quantity:')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'Remove' })).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'Edit' })).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.queryByText('Ship to store')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  ```
  This is a real DOM-absence check, not merely "doesn't throw" — the `queryBy*`/`.not.toBeInTheDocument()` assertions are the actual proof.

  **(b) Omitted-prop / backward-compat test**, lines 189–203 (`'every existing caller (hideStepperAndActions omitted) is unaffected — the stepper and actions still render'`):
  ```tsx
  renderWithProviders(
    <ProductItem
      product={MOCK_LINE_ITEM}
      primaryAction={<button type="button">Remove</button>}
      secondaryActions={<button type="button">Edit</button>}
      deliveryActions={<span>Ship to store</span>}
    />,
  );

  expect(screen.getByText('Quantity:')).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getAllByRole('button', { name: 'Remove' }).length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
  expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Edit' })).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getAllByText('Ship to store').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
  ```
  Positive presence assertion, confirmed. Note it correctly uses `getAllByText`/`getAllByRole` for `deliveryActions`/`primaryAction` (each renders twice, once per breakpoint) and singular `getBy*` for `secondaryActions` (renders once) — internally consistent with the two-render-site structure in index.tsx.

  ## 3. GiftCard story — index.stories.tsx:173–180

  ```tsx
  export const GiftCard: Story = {
    args: {
      product: MOCK_LINE_ITEM,
      primaryAction: <button type="button">Remove</button>,
      secondaryActions: <button type="button">Edit</button>,
      hideStepperAndActions: true,
    },
  };
  ```
  Exists, passes `hideStepperAndActions: true`, confirmed.

  **Minor finding (doc-accuracy only, not a coverage gap):** the inline comment directly above the story (lines 170–172) claims `primaryAction`/`secondaryActions`/`deliveryActions` are "still passed here deliberately, to prove they are suppressed" — but the story's `args` only sets `primaryAction` and `secondaryActions`; `deliveryActions` is not passed (and `meta.args` doesn't default it either), so it's actually `undefined` in this story, not "passed and suppressed." This does not undermine the claim under test — the actual proof that `deliveryActions` is suppressed by the prop lives in index.test.tsx §2(a) above, which does pass a real `deliveryActions` node and asserts its absence. This is just a one-line comment overclaiming what this specific story demonstrates.

  ## 4. Real vitest run

  ```
  $ npx vitest run overrides/app/components/product-item/index.test.tsx
   ✓ overrides/app/components/product-item/index.test.tsx (3 tests) 288ms
   Test Files  1 passed (1)
        Tests  3 passed (3)
  ```
  All 3 tests pass (the "Could not parse CSS stylesheet" lines are pre-existing jsdom stderr noise, not test failures).

  ## 5. Mutation test — proving the suppression test has real teeth (not just coincidentally passing)

  Since the task called out the two-`deliveryActions`-sites case as the most likely place for an incomplete fix to hide, I didn't just trust the passing suite — I deliberately reintroduced that exact bug to confirm the test would actually catch it. I removed the `!hideStepperAndActions &&` guard from only the second site (line 179–181, `HideOnDesktop`), leaving the first site (`HideOnMobile`) correctly gated, then reran the suite:

  ```
  ❯ overrides/app/components/product-item/index.test.tsx (3 tests | 1 failed)
     ✓ ProductItem > renders the image with an alt, the name uppercase, the price, and one combined colour+size node
     × ProductItem > hideStepperAndActions suppresses the stepper and every actions surface, and nothing throws
       expected document not to contain element, found <span>
    Ship to store
  </span> instead
     ✓ ProductItem > every existing caller (hideStepperAndActions omitted) is unaffected — the stepper and actions still render
  ```
  The suppression test failed immediately and specifically on the correct assertion (`screen.queryByText('Ship to store')`), proving it would genuinely catch a partial-gating regression on either `deliveryActions` site. I then restored the file from a pre-mutation backup and verified byte-for-byte identity (`diff` reported no differences) plus reran the full suite clean (3/3 passing again). `git status`/`git diff --stat` on the file afterward match the pre-existing working-tree state noted at session start — no residual change from this verification step.

  **Bottom line: the claim is CONFIRMED as stated** — the prop is boolean/optional, both `deliveryActions` render sites are gated (the specific failure mode I was asked to hunt for is not present), the stepper/primaryAction (both sites)/secondaryActions are also gated, both required tests exist with real DOM-presence/absence assertions and pass, the `GiftCard` story exists and uses the prop, and the real vitest run is green. Only a cosmetic one-line comment overclaim in index.stories.tsx (noted above) is worth a mention to the Implementer, not a re-open.
